---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Percentage-Based Programming | 1rmaxcalculator.com';
const description = 'How to use your one rep max to plan strength training. Percentage zones, rep schemes, weekly structure, and common program templates.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>Percentage-Based Programming</h1>
  <p>Once you have a reliable 1RM, you can program training around percentages of it. This is how the majority of intermediate and advanced strength programs work.</p>

  <h2>Standard percentage zones</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>% of 1RM</th><th>Reps per set</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>50&ndash;65%</td><td>10&ndash;15+</td><td>Warm-up, technique, recovery work</td></tr>
      <tr><td>65&ndash;75%</td><td>6&ndash;12</td><td>Hypertrophy</td></tr>
      <tr><td>75&ndash;85%</td><td>3&ndash;6</td><td>Strength</td></tr>
      <tr><td>85&ndash;92%</td><td>2&ndash;4</td><td>Heavy strength / peaking</td></tr>
      <tr><td>92&ndash;100%</td><td>1&ndash;2</td><td>Singles, max testing</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Weekly structure</h2>
  <p>A common intermediate template:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Heavy day:</strong> 85&ndash;90% for 3&ndash;5 sets of 1&ndash;3 reps</li>
    <li><strong>Volume day:</strong> 70&ndash;80% for 4&ndash;6 sets of 5&ndash;8 reps</li>
    <li><strong>Light day:</strong> 60&ndash;70% for 3&ndash;5 sets of 5&ndash;10 reps with technique focus</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to recalculate</h2>
  <p>Every 4&ndash;8 weeks, after a clear PR set. Don't recalculate after every good day &mdash; that creates inflation that eventually catches up with you.</p>

  <p>For peak preparation, see our <a href="/guides/peaking-block-strength">peaking blocks guide</a>.</p>

  <style>
    table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1rem 0; }
    th, td { padding: 0.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); text-align: left; }
    th { background: #f6f6f6; }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
